{"name":"Dry Lichen","hex":"#c7d9cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Darai."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Free from or lacking moisture.","Unable to produce a liquid, as water,  oil, or  milk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dry"},{"term":"lichen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of many symbiotic organisms, being associations of algae and fungi, often found as white or yellow-to-blue–green patches on rocks, old walls, etc.","Something which gradually spreads across something else, causing damage."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with lichen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lichen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lichen","blocks":[{"text":"A lichen is a hybrid colony of algae or cyanobacteria living symbiotically among filaments of multiple fungus species, along with bacteria embedded in the cortex, or \"skin\", in a mutualistic relationship. Lichens are the lifeform that first brought the term symbiosis into biological context."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Letharia_vulpina_JHollinger_crop.jpg/330px-Letharia_vulpina_JHollinger_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lichen"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Flavoparmelia_caperata_-_Flickr_-_pellaea_%287%29.jpg/500px-Flavoparmelia_caperata_-_Flickr_-_pellaea_%287%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Flavoparmelia_caperata_-_Flickr_-_pellaea_%287%29.jpg/1280px-Flavoparmelia_caperata_-_Flickr_-_pellaea_%287%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Flavoparmelia_caperata_-_Flickr_-_pellaea_%28